I need a tiny unified-diff parser for old-side changed lines and new-side. Simpler: parse with `patch --dry-run` combined. Let me implement:

```python
def changed_old_lines(patch_text):
    lines = patch_text.splitlines()
    out=set(); old_no=None
    for ln in lines:
        m=re.match(r"^@@ -(\d+)(?:,\d+)? \+\d+(?:,\d+)? @@", ln)
        if m: old_no=int(m.group(1)); continue
        if old_no is None: continue
        if ln.startswith('---') or ln.startswith('+++'): continue
        if ln.startswith('-'): out.add(old_no); old_no+=1
        elif ln.startswith('+'): pass
        elif ln.startswith(' '): old_no+=1
        elif ln.startswith('\\'): pass
    return out
```

